WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:11.990 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hello and welcome back to playstation  grenade  so the next gen consoles are finally  here the xbox series x and my personal  bae  the ps5 so i decided to compare the ps4  user experience  to that of the new and improved ps5  to see what exactly has changed between  these console generations on fortnite  and i gotta say i'm impressed i'm gonna  break down everything i've noticed on  ps5 but keep in mind these are on xbox  series x2  you play wherever you wanna play no  shade throwing here  if you'd like to support me please think  about using code adamarrow in the store  but if not a like  would be much appreciated here's a ton  of changes you should know when you take  the step  into the next generation  so let's start with the battle bus and  likely the first thing you'll notice  when you see the island  are those new cloud formations  volumetric clouds  i never thought i'd be so happy to see a  cloud update in fortnite  but i am check out how the clouds  dissipate naturally  and i've also noticed there are far more  clouds when you are in a game on ps5  compared to ps4  even when it's the exact same match it's  when you see the whole map from the sky  that this  minor update looks phenomenal during my  tests i noticed that the night sky  was even more vibrant now with more  levels of contrast over the ps4 version  and everything just pops a little more  next let's look at those campfires  here's what lighting a fire used to look  like on ps4  nice looks good right well check it out  on the ps5 update  that is lit puns the smoke gathers and  the fire burns  in incredible detail the light given off  slightly illuminates the area close by  those effects were here on ps4 and xbox  one  but now on next gen lighting and  elemental effects  are insane  [Music]  next the storm whilst running around in  game i noticed the clouds as the storm  gathers in the distance and it's changed  i'll switch between ps4 and 5 to  demonstrate this  basically the storm has additional  colours which gather over time  the new purple sections really grab your  attention and make the storm much more  daunting as it approaches i've seen some  mighty fine looking  pink clouds forming where the ps4 keeps  to the og white and purple approach  i then decided to sit and wait for the  storm wall to move in  first on ps4 the animation we're used to  it's always been  quite difficult to know where the storm  starts due to the color being very  subtle  we usually look at a tree in the  distance and watch the storm cover it  with blue light then as the wall gets  close enough the small squares become  apparent  and the blue and purple colours even out  well on ps5  we have a key difference here the storm  wall now has squares upon it from  distance  right from the outset it's now easy to  spot from any place on the map  as the squares grow over the objects in  the distance  these squares then subtly fade away when  near and the wall becomes the same one  as last generation  here's a super small change i almost  missed completely  whilst opening a loot llama which  doesn't seem to have a new animation by  the way  take a look at the shield pot that pops  out on the ps4 it has a shadow  underneath  whereas now on ps5 this is a glowing pot  giving out a light source  how great is that super subtle but a  great update all the same  [Music]  next let's address the foliage around  the island when running around you'll  notice  far more blades of grass and plants and  stones everywhere  these are most obvious around dirt  tracks and near water edges  this really is part of a bigger texture  update because now the trees are much  more detailed and defined from the  quality of the ps4 days  of course the new gen stuff loads much  quicker thanks to those ssds  which means the render distance in game  now is monumental  which means now there's much less chance  you'll get the unrendered buildings in  the distance which look like  melted toast and this can also be seen  with the new volumetric lighting  look at penny's shoulders here look at  the edges of her suit  the light hits these sections and  illuminates the character and makes them  pop from the background even more than  before  and this is everywhere you go the  lighting on next-gen is exquisite with  darker areas more defined  and brighter areas piercing through the  haze  it's impressive work okay here's a very  strange one but i like it do you ever  frolick in the water  okay keep that to yourself on ps4 the  interactions with the water is quite  minimal  here i am jumping around like a fool  whereas on ps5  it looks like this notice how the  character interrupts the bubbles on the  water top and breaks through that flow  it's another completely pointless  addition but it's great all the same  the immersion this offers is usually  only available to high-end pc  players but now console gamers have the  same visual effects to enjoy  oh and this goes even further check this  out in shallow water the physics have  changed  come watch me for a look again these are  dynamic ripples on the ps5 and xbox  series x  whereas last gen is left without any in  the replay files on ps5 i noticed that  these  real-time effects don't actually carry  over and the water remains lifeless  it's a shame for those people who make  cinematic videos  but it just means that if you want to  enjoy this goodness it has to be in a  live match  anyway this is far too much talking  about me jumping around in water  let's move on on to something  less great now sadly those expecting to  see ray tracing on the new consoles  on day one at least will be a little  upset to confirm ray tracing is how  light reflects from  objects for the biggest example of this  we tend to look at windows with our  characters to see what looks back at us  on ps5 the reflections remain the same  as last generation  and if you look closely the reflection  is actually our character as seen on  screen  which is why you can spot your own back  bling in windows  so right now ray tracing isn't here but  it is on the way  i'll let you know in a map change video  when that happens let's go back to fire  again  i decided to burn down a tree to check  what happens  on the ps4 everything goes as planned as  you'd expect  but on the ps5 check out the flames the  flames are visibly improved and the  burning around the trees is much more  ferocious too  [Music]  other random things i've noticed include  bigger mushrooms on ps5  it's strange but true and check out the  cool added effect  to chug splashes on ps5 a particle  effect is added  to the splash zone check out the bush  here  the particles literally drip off the  edge wow  we really are in the next generation  dripping bushes  for our next treat i had fun with  explosives  and found some more changes here are the  ps4s booms and explosions  very nice but now on ps5 those  explosions have been increased  with once again the smoke effects really  adding to the intensity again  same with the grenades and other  [Music]  projectiles  the grenades in particular look way more  meaty now on next-gen hardware  and check out the trails on a rocket in  [Music]  motion  now that looks cinematic whilst testing  all this i noticed the new particle  animation when a player is eliminated  we are all used to the player  deconstructing and vanishing into fresh  air  but now on ps5 these have been once  again increased  everything is simply more impactful just  look at the detail of it breaking away  [Music]  another thing you may like to know is  what happens when we win a game  once we win on ps4 a few pieces of paper  ticker tape flutter around in the sky  and we are proclaimed vic royce well on  ps5  there is more ticker tape yeah that's it  strange but true i do hope  it's biodegradable  it should be noted that the ps5  controller supports haptic feedback when  shooting which means when you have a  sniper in hand  you'll have to press the trigger down  much harder to fire  it tries to replicate real life this is  awful for competitive gamers  but for those who want immersion you'll  be very happy here  whilst editing this i noticed another  subtle but impactful  change lens flare depending on the time  of day it's possible to see the sun or  moonlight reflect from surfaces  you may think that's nothing new but  just look how this horrible swamp  changes with a little bit of lens flare  added to the camera  i really should have shot this by the  ocean i don't know why i'm choosing  shrek swamp so there we have it 20  changes in the fortnite next gen update  some are huge like fire and water and  others are quite subtle like the  lighting and the improved render  distances  overall the game runs like a dream on  next-gen consoles  i can only vouch for the ps5 but i'm  told the xbox series x is just as  fantastic  anyway thanks for your time and has that  uh  thing stuck in your head because it  really has stuck in mine on screen now  i'm more of those leggings who are kind  enough to use code adamaru in the  fortnite shop these guys sent me a  twitter dm to approve their purchase  and i name them because they are  leggings tada  thank you very much for supporting me  i'm adam from playstation grenade you're  awesome  and i'll see you next time  [Music]

